From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:55:39 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: remove the load spreader and the lines it raised on

The load spreader takes descriptors the dequeue manager sends to the
processor and distributes them over four output rings, one per hardware
thread, each raising its own interrupt line. Four of the manager's five
interrupt handlers exist only to mask their line and hand the ring to a
bottom half, and the bottom half exists only to drain it.

Nothing sends the processor a descriptor that way any more. The network
device that drives this datapath receives on its macro's DMA ring
instead, and the previous change removed the delivery tail that was the
drained ring's only consumer, so the rings have no producer and no
consumer left.

Remove the bring-up, the four handlers, the drain, the bottom half and
the register block they shared, and stop claiming the four interrupt
lines. Their enables are now written to zero explicitly instead of being
left at whatever reset put there: the lines are level-sourced, and
masking them at the source is what makes it safe for no handler to be
registered.

What stays is the line the free-segment queue managers and the
processor's own enqueue and dequeue ports raise on. Those ports are live
- the network device enqueues through them and returns segments through
them - and the free-segment managers report violations that have no other
witness.

The two controller enables keep their order across the removal, and the
dequeue ports the manager preconfigures are untouched.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

